„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÈSurely none of the men that came up out of Egypt, from twenty years old and upward, shall see the land which I sware unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob; because they have not wholly followed me:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpsave Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite, and Joshua the son of Nun: for they have wholly followed the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼And the LORD's anger was kindled against Israel, and he made them wander in the wilderness forty years, until all the generation, that had done evil in the sight of the LORD, was consumed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd, behold, ye are risen up in your fathers' stead, an increase of sinful men, to augment yet the fierce anger of the LORD toward Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyFor if ye turn away from after him, he will yet again leave them in the wilderness; and ye shall destroy all this people.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAnd they came near unto him, and said, We will build sheepfolds here for our cattle, and cities for our little ones:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍbut we ourselves will go ready armed before the children of Israel, until we have brought them unto their place: and our little ones shall dwell in the fenced cities because of the inhabitants of the land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjWe will not return unto our houses, until the children of Israel have inherited every man his inheritance.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠFor we will not inherit with them on yonder side Jordan, or forward; because our inheritance is fallen to us on this side Jordan eastward.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And Moses said unto them, If ye will do this thing, if ye will go armed before the LORD to war,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoand will go all of you armed over Jordan before the LORD, until he hath driven out his enemies from before him,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµand the land be subdued before the LORD: then afterward ye shall return, and be guiltless before the LORD, and before Israel; and this land shall be your possession before the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjBut if ye will not do so, behold, ye have sinned against the LORD: and be sure your sin will find you out.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtBuild you cities for your little ones, and folds for your sheep; and do that which hath proceeded out of your mouth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAnd the children of Gad and the children of Reuben spake unto Moses, saying, Thy servants will do as my lord commandeth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcOur little ones, our wives, our flocks, and all our cattle, shall be there in the cities of Gilead:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfbut thy servants will pass over, every man armed for war, before the LORD to battle, as my lord saith.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSo concerning them Moses commanded Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun, and the chief fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙşand Moses said unto them, If the children of Gad and the children of Reuben will pass with you over Jordan, every man armed to battle, before the LORD, and the land shall be subdued before you; then ye shall give them the land of Gilead for a possession:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkbut if they will not pass over with you armed, they shall have possessions among you in the land of Canaan.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|And the children of Gad and the children of Reuben answered, saying, As the LORD hath said unto thy servants, so will we do.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰We will pass over armed before the LORD into the land of Canaan, that the possession of our inheritance on this side Jordan may be our's.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter «first_verse!ªlast_verse&¦verses–„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ:And Moses gave unto them, even to the children of Gad, and to the children of Reuben, and unto half the tribe of Manasseh the son of Joseph, the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites, and the kingdom of Og king of Bashan, the land, with the cities thereof in the coasts, even the cities of the country round about.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<And the children of Gad built Dibon, and Ataroth, and Aroer,¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.and Atroth, Shophan, and Jaazer, and Jogbehah,¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDand Beth-nimrah, and Beth-haran, fenced cities: and folds for sheep.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFAnd the children of Reuben built Heshbon, and Elealeh, and Kirjathaim,¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{and Nebo, and Baal-meon, (their names being changed,) and Shibmah: and gave other names unto the cities which they builded.¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book§chapter «first_verse'ªlast_verse*¦verses”„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd the children of Machir the son of Manasseh went to Gilead, and took it, and dispossessed the Amorite which was in it.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLAnd Moses gave Gilead unto Machir the son of Manasseh; and he dwelt therein.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And Jair the son of Manasseh went and took the small towns thereof, and called them Havoth-jair.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd Nobah went and took Kenath, and the villages thereof, and called it Nobah, after his own name.¦layout ªlast_verse*